Fig. 8A shows that in -15% of the preparations, a concentration-dependent shrinkage was observed with ATP alone (N-4, P < 0.01). The values generated by the fits were: v∞ = 94.3+0.3% and τ = 2.8±0.7min (10μM ATP), and 

 2.8±0.7min (100μM ATP). Fig. 8B shows the combined effect of tamoxifen (TMX) and ATP on suspensions responding to ATP alone. The presence of 10μM tamoxifen enhanced the response to both 3μM (P < 0.01) and 10μM ATP (P < 0.05). The values of the fits were: v∞ - 98.0±0.4%, τ - 10.8±4.9min (3μM ATP alone); v∞ - 96.7+0.4%, τ = 5.8±2.1min (3μM ATP+ 10μM TMX); 

 1.6±1.0min (10μM ATP alone); 

 - 95.7+0.3%, τ = 1.4±0.7min (10μM ATP+ 10μM TMX). Fig. 8C shows the dependence of synergistic shrinkage on ATP concentration. Tamoxifen (6μM) was present throughout (N = 5). Shrinkage was observed in the simultaneous presence of 10μM or 1mM ATP (P< 0.01), but not at 1 μM ATP. The data obtained at 10μM and 1mM ATP were not significantly different from each another. The fit obtained at 10μM ATP was characterized by v^ = 95.7+0.7% and τ =6.6+3.2min.
